1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kisskh.asia =

2
00:00:07,665 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

3
00:01:35,425 --> 00:01:38,945
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

4
00:02:22,145 --> 00:02:25,185
SNOW FALLS WITH YOU BESIDE ME

5
00:02:35,865 --> 00:02:37,865
LUAN NIAN

6
00:02:43,305 --> 00:02:44,145
Open the door.

7
00:03:05,345 --> 00:03:07,025
We're going to the hospital.

8
00:03:13,105 --> 00:03:14,185
I'm not going.

9
00:03:33,625 --> 00:03:36,025
Your face is burning red,
and you won't go to the hospital?

10
00:03:36,105 --> 00:03:37,185
Do you have a death wish?

11
00:04:16,225 --> 00:04:17,745
I really don't need to go to the hospital.

12
00:04:18,705 --> 00:04:20,345
I'll be fine after some rest.

13
00:04:22,985 --> 00:04:23,825
Fine.

14
00:04:24,345 --> 00:04:26,785
I'll check the company system
for your emergency contact

15
00:04:27,345 --> 00:04:29,465
and inform your family.

16
00:04:29,545 --> 00:04:32,425
If you suffer any complications
or accidents later,

17
00:04:32,505 --> 00:04:33,345
the company won't be liable.

18
00:04:47,505 --> 00:04:48,705
Your hand's burning.

19
00:05:08,785 --> 00:05:11,025
Stop being stubborn. Let's go.

20
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:45,145
The doctor said it was a mild case
of mycoplasma pneumonia.

21
00:05:45,745 --> 00:05:47,705
A cough and a slight fever.

22
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,665
Some congee should be fine, right?

23
00:05:52,625 --> 00:05:54,625
It's not me. I'm asking for a friend.

24
00:05:56,025 --> 00:05:56,945
Thanks.

25
00:05:58,345 --> 00:05:59,865
Thank you, Dr. Liang.

26
00:07:06,185 --> 00:07:07,065
You're awake.

27
00:07:08,505 --> 00:07:09,345
Come eat.

28
00:07:26,385 --> 00:07:27,705
Thank you, Mr. Luan.

29
00:07:30,625 --> 00:07:31,505
Drop the formalities.

30
00:07:32,425 --> 00:07:34,665
Don't you get tired
of addressing me like that?

31
00:07:36,585 --> 00:07:37,465
I…

32
00:07:47,905 --> 00:07:49,145
Did you burn your hand?

33
00:07:49,905 --> 00:07:50,785
Did you put anything on it?

34
00:07:51,785 --> 00:07:54,305
Don't worry about it. Eat.

35
00:07:58,625 --> 00:07:59,945
I'm feeling much better.

36
00:08:00,745 --> 00:08:02,385
Could you take me home?

37
00:08:03,225 --> 00:08:04,385
I don't want to impose.

38
00:08:06,105 --> 00:08:07,025
Why are you acting like a stranger?

39
00:08:14,665 --> 00:08:16,225
We dated, after all.

40
00:08:16,305 --> 00:08:18,745
You don't need to feel bad
about letting me take care of you.

41
00:08:24,865 --> 00:08:25,985
I want to go home.

42
00:08:27,945 --> 00:08:28,785
I want…

43
00:08:33,985 --> 00:08:35,545
to end this relationship.

44
00:08:41,225 --> 00:08:42,105
We can.

45
00:08:46,225 --> 00:08:47,225
Once you're better.

46
00:09:00,625 --> 00:09:03,745
Later, when I looked back
on who I was then,

47
00:09:04,745 --> 00:09:09,345
I couldn't explain
why I made that decision.

48
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:15,185
Why do people always do
such foolish things

49
00:09:15,265 --> 00:09:16,665
when they're young?

50
00:09:20,665 --> 00:09:24,705
How could something
that began like that ever end well?

51
00:09:26,265 --> 00:09:30,745
I acted as if foolish choices
came without a price.

52
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:43,825
You sweated from the fever.

53
00:09:43,905 --> 00:09:45,145
Go take a shower.

54
00:09:45,945 --> 00:09:48,465
You need proper rest to recover.

55
00:09:54,905 --> 00:09:55,905
Come on.

56
00:10:08,705 --> 00:10:11,065
Did you prepare all this for me?

57
00:10:13,785 --> 00:10:14,785
Other women left them here.

58
00:10:16,265 --> 00:10:17,865
Label them when you use them.

59
00:10:18,385 --> 00:10:20,945
That way, the next woman who comes over

60
00:10:21,985 --> 00:10:23,585
won't use or wear the wrong things.

61
00:10:26,185 --> 00:10:27,745
These match my prescription.

62
00:10:29,185 --> 00:10:30,265
What a coincidence.

63
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:00,105
Come sit down.

64
00:11:15,505 --> 00:11:16,625
What are you covering up?

65
00:11:17,185 --> 00:11:18,225
I've seen it all before.

66
00:11:22,905 --> 00:11:25,425
Why are you always so cutting?

67
00:11:27,145 --> 00:11:29,425
Are you like this with everyone
or only with me?

68
00:11:49,385 --> 00:11:53,705
You only said you wanted to end things
because you were angry, right?

69
00:11:57,665 --> 00:11:58,905
I meant it.

70
00:12:05,585 --> 00:12:06,425
Really?

71
00:12:38,545 --> 00:12:39,625
It's snowing.

72
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:08,625
Let's go watch it.

73
00:13:34,065 --> 00:13:34,905
It's cold.

74
00:13:37,465 --> 00:13:38,345
Don't end this.

75
00:13:39,065 --> 00:13:40,665
Or we'll freeze
into ice sculptures together.

76
00:13:50,185 --> 00:13:51,625
Could you be more childish?

77
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:52,825
I'm still sick.

78
00:13:55,785 --> 00:13:57,225
Then don't break up with me.

79
00:14:28,305 --> 00:14:31,385
There were so many gift boxes
in your trunk.

80
00:14:32,545 --> 00:14:34,545
Were they meant for other women?

81
00:14:40,905 --> 00:14:41,945
Shang Zhitao,

82
00:14:42,905 --> 00:14:46,305
do you know how
luxury-brand pre-spend works?

83
00:14:55,705 --> 00:14:58,745
I don't want to know anything,
including you.

84
00:15:06,185 --> 00:15:08,865
You can take your time getting
to know me once you're better.

85
00:15:25,705 --> 00:15:26,825
SHAANXI GUOKUI BUNS

86
00:15:26,905 --> 00:15:27,745
Mom.

87
00:15:29,145 --> 00:15:30,625
Did you get the buns?

88
00:15:30,705 --> 00:15:32,785
I did. They're delicious.

89
00:15:33,505 --> 00:15:35,585
We don't have much worth sending.

90
00:15:36,105 --> 00:15:37,345
But I know you like them,

91
00:15:37,425 --> 00:15:40,905
so I sent extra for you
to share with your roommates.

92
00:15:40,985 --> 00:15:42,185
Is it enough?

93
00:15:42,265 --> 00:15:44,625
Yes. Don't worry.

94
00:15:44,705 --> 00:15:46,025
About the house,

95
00:15:46,985 --> 00:15:48,465
your father still thinks we should buy it.

96
00:15:50,025 --> 00:15:51,905
Your sister's grown up.

97
00:15:51,985 --> 00:15:53,425
It really isn't convenient.

98
00:15:54,465 --> 00:15:57,025
Mom, what about the money
I just sent home?

99
00:15:57,825 --> 00:15:59,025
Did Dad take it again?

100
00:15:59,105 --> 00:16:01,265
Give me the phone. I'll talk to him.

101
00:16:02,545 --> 00:16:05,265
Listen. That place has a lot of buyers,

102
00:16:05,345 --> 00:16:06,425
and it's a bargain.

103
00:16:06,505 --> 00:16:08,905
We won't get another chance like this.

104
00:16:08,985 --> 00:16:10,825
I'm still 30,000 yuan short.
Send it over right away.

105
00:16:10,905 --> 00:16:13,025
Don't talk to him like that.

106
00:16:13,105 --> 00:16:15,825
I know life in Beijing isn't easy for you,

107
00:16:16,905 --> 00:16:18,945
but we want to buy a bigger place

108
00:16:19,025 --> 00:16:20,905
and put it
in your and your sister's names.

109
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:23,185
That way, you'll both
have something to fall back on.

110
00:16:23,265 --> 00:16:24,785
Don't bother explaining.

111
00:16:24,865 --> 00:16:26,025
Tell him to send the money now.

112
00:16:26,105 --> 00:16:27,545
Hang up and go cook.

113
00:16:42,025 --> 00:16:45,545
TRANSFER: RMB 30,000

114
00:16:49,585 --> 00:16:51,705
TRANSFER SUCCESSFUL

115
00:17:09,505 --> 00:17:11,665
What? Pneumonia?

116
00:17:11,745 --> 00:17:12,944
Are you OK?

117
00:17:13,025 --> 00:17:15,184
Yes. I'm almost recovered.

118
00:17:15,265 --> 00:17:18,345
So you're staying at Luan Nian's now?

119
00:17:19,745 --> 00:17:20,865
Are you two back together?

120
00:17:20,944 --> 00:17:22,424
I'VE GONE TO THE SUPERMARKET
I'LL BE BACK SOON

121
00:17:26,265 --> 00:17:27,825
He's been taking good care of me.

122
00:17:28,345 --> 00:17:29,785
He's done everything he can.

123
00:17:30,905 --> 00:17:33,425
He rushed back
to take care of you, his girlfriend.

124
00:17:33,985 --> 00:17:35,985
He is into you.

125
00:17:37,305 --> 00:17:39,985
I can't bring myself to ask
about him and Zang Yao.

126
00:17:43,865 --> 00:17:44,945
I'll leave it at that.

127
00:17:45,665 --> 00:17:47,225
I don't want to dig any deeper.

128
00:17:49,705 --> 00:17:50,825
Take your time.

129
00:17:51,705 --> 00:17:54,465
Some things can't be rushed.

130
00:17:54,545 --> 00:17:59,425
Leaving some questions unasked may
make a relationship last longer, right?

131
00:18:00,865 --> 00:18:01,825
You're right.

132
00:18:05,025 --> 00:18:07,785
I have to go. I think he's back.

133
00:18:48,465 --> 00:18:50,025
Your friend's here.

134
00:18:51,625 --> 00:18:53,145
Why are you here?

135
00:18:59,585 --> 00:19:00,985
Drinking in broad daylight?

136
00:19:01,065 --> 00:19:04,225
Why can't I? I drink when I feel like it.

137
00:19:05,905 --> 00:19:06,905
Want some?

138
00:19:07,945 --> 00:19:08,785
I…

139
00:19:09,465 --> 00:19:11,625
-I should go home.
-Why?

140
00:19:16,025 --> 00:19:16,905
Are you fully recovered?

141
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:21,905
I'll make you some soup later.

142
00:19:23,705 --> 00:19:26,105
It'd be awkward with me here.

143
00:19:29,785 --> 00:19:30,905
She's the one who's intruding.

144
00:19:37,505 --> 00:19:39,145
So she's your new girlfriend?

145
00:19:40,825 --> 00:19:42,025
-Yes.
-No.

146
00:19:47,585 --> 00:19:50,065
You two really aren't on the same page.

147
00:19:53,865 --> 00:19:56,025
Maybe you should change
the water in the tank.

148
00:19:56,625 --> 00:19:57,625
Why?

149
00:19:58,865 --> 00:20:00,105
She threw up in it.

150
00:20:02,145 --> 00:20:03,465
Zang Yao.

151
00:20:16,105 --> 00:20:17,905
Shang Zhitao.

152
00:20:17,985 --> 00:20:19,505
That's a pretty name.

153
00:20:24,385 --> 00:20:25,625
How do you put up with Luan Nian?

154
00:20:25,705 --> 00:20:26,945
Look at him.

155
00:20:27,025 --> 00:20:30,225
Even at home, he looks like
he's chairing a board meeting.

156
00:20:32,625 --> 00:20:35,305
What kind of rare fish
is it that you treasure so much?

157
00:20:35,385 --> 00:20:37,825
If it dies, I'll buy you ten more.

158
00:20:38,985 --> 00:20:41,425
If you can't make conversation, say less.

159
00:20:42,345 --> 00:20:43,985
Hongqi is his baby.

160
00:20:44,065 --> 00:20:45,705
Sometimes he talks to it.

161
00:20:47,305 --> 00:20:48,145
What are you talking about?

162
00:20:48,785 --> 00:20:52,345
I heard you. You told it to swim faster.

163
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,185
We've known each other for over 20 years.

164
00:20:58,265 --> 00:21:01,145
He's always been quiet
and never liked talking much.

165
00:21:01,225 --> 00:21:03,145
So he's been confiding in his fish.

166
00:21:03,225 --> 00:21:06,465
I've been away so long
that I understand you less and less.

167
00:21:09,305 --> 00:21:10,385
How about this?

168
00:21:10,465 --> 00:21:14,065
Let's play a game we used to play as kids.

169
00:21:14,145 --> 00:21:16,105
Rock-paper-scissors, then questions.

170
00:21:16,185 --> 00:21:18,625
Whoever loses can either answer a question

171
00:21:18,705 --> 00:21:19,985
or take a flick to the forehead.

172
00:21:21,265 --> 00:21:22,385
You know how to play, right?

173
00:21:23,865 --> 00:21:26,145
Come on. Rock, paper, scissors.

174
00:21:30,985 --> 00:21:31,825
You first.

175
00:21:32,505 --> 00:21:33,785
Why did you suddenly come back to China?

176
00:21:33,865 --> 00:21:36,785
I broke up with my British boyfriend.

177
00:21:36,865 --> 00:21:39,185
Then I met a guy from Guangzhou
and followed him there.

178
00:21:39,785 --> 00:21:40,865
You certainly kept busy.

179
00:21:42,465 --> 00:21:45,425
Will you take a flick to the forehead
or answer a question?

180
00:21:46,465 --> 00:21:47,465
I'll answer a question.

181
00:21:50,425 --> 00:21:51,825
Is anyone pursuing you right now?

182
00:21:54,465 --> 00:21:55,305
No.

183
00:21:57,745 --> 00:21:59,185
That's normal. Nothing to be ashamed of.

184
00:22:00,305 --> 00:22:04,425
Some people go their whole lives
without anyone ever pursuing them.

185
00:22:08,825 --> 00:22:10,145
I have been pursued.

186
00:22:11,305 --> 00:22:12,745
My ex-boyfriend loved me very much.

187
00:22:12,825 --> 00:22:14,625
Then why did he break up with you?

188
00:22:17,505 --> 00:22:19,665
-Again.
-Come on.

189
00:22:20,265 --> 00:22:21,425
Rock, paper, scissors.

190
00:22:23,185 --> 00:22:24,025
You again.

191
00:22:26,065 --> 00:22:27,105
Still answering a question?

192
00:22:29,025 --> 00:22:29,825
I'll take the flick.

193
00:22:29,905 --> 00:22:31,625
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

194
00:22:40,505 --> 00:22:41,345
Come here.

195
00:22:46,705 --> 00:22:48,425
What's wrong? You chose the flick.

196
00:22:49,025 --> 00:22:51,025
I didn't think you'd flick me that hard.

197
00:22:52,345 --> 00:22:54,065
When we were kids,
Luan Nian could flick my forehead

198
00:22:54,145 --> 00:22:55,905
hard enough to send an eraser flying.

199
00:22:55,985 --> 00:22:57,825
He never went easy on girls.

200
00:22:59,265 --> 00:23:01,065
I thought you'd go easier on me.

201
00:23:02,545 --> 00:23:03,505
Let me see.

202
00:23:04,785 --> 00:23:05,705
I'm fine.

203
00:23:07,345 --> 00:23:08,225
There, there.

204
00:23:10,065 --> 00:23:11,825
Again. Come on.

205
00:23:12,465 --> 00:23:13,905
Rock, paper, scissors.

206
00:23:20,145 --> 00:23:21,945
You know Luan Nian

207
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:23,905
has a crescent-shaped scar
on his left leg, right?

208
00:23:25,665 --> 00:23:26,705
He…

209
00:23:27,265 --> 00:23:28,345
He does?

210
00:23:28,865 --> 00:23:31,065
-Do you know how he got it?
-From running.

211
00:23:32,105 --> 00:23:33,105
Nonsense.

212
00:23:33,185 --> 00:23:35,465
When I was seven, I took you
climbing a wall to raid a bird's nest.

213
00:23:35,545 --> 00:23:36,745
Zang Yao.

214
00:23:37,385 --> 00:23:39,905
Fine. I'll talk about something else.

215
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:40,825
His mom said

216
00:23:40,905 --> 00:23:44,025
that by the time he was seven or eight,
he already acted like a grown-up,

217
00:23:44,105 --> 00:23:45,145
always frowning,

218
00:23:45,865 --> 00:23:48,385
never truly interested in anything,
and impossible to please.

219
00:23:48,985 --> 00:23:53,025
You're nothing like Dr. Liang
or your father.

220
00:23:53,105 --> 00:23:54,745
Were you adopted?

221
00:24:00,665 --> 00:24:01,665
How about another round?

222
00:24:03,105 --> 00:24:04,265
Sure.

223
00:24:04,345 --> 00:24:05,905
Rock, paper, scissors.

224
00:24:08,105 --> 00:24:08,945
Forehead flick.

225
00:24:27,145 --> 00:24:27,985
That was gentle.

226
00:24:39,345 --> 00:24:40,945
When are you two getting married?

227
00:24:42,025 --> 00:24:43,225
We don't have any plans yet.

228
00:24:45,265 --> 00:24:46,385
I'm warning you.

229
00:24:46,465 --> 00:24:48,025
Don't say anything to my mom.

230
00:24:49,425 --> 00:24:52,385
I was asking on Dr. Liang's behalf.

231
00:24:52,465 --> 00:24:54,265
Really. She's always asking me
to set you up with someone.

232
00:24:54,945 --> 00:24:56,065
She says with your personality,

233
00:24:56,145 --> 00:24:57,585
you'll bottle everything up
until it kills you.

234
00:25:12,465 --> 00:25:13,545
Boring.

235
00:25:16,865 --> 00:25:20,425
Well, I hope you two make it all the way.

236
00:25:33,025 --> 00:25:34,985
I'm meeting my girls at the bar. Bye.

237
00:26:05,505 --> 00:26:07,185
I only wanted us to be family

238
00:26:08,505 --> 00:26:09,665
and best friends.

239
00:26:58,785 --> 00:26:59,745
Take your medicine.

240
00:27:08,665 --> 00:27:11,545
When your ex flicked you on the forehead,
was he gentler than I was?

241
00:27:20,705 --> 00:27:22,705
I don't know you as well as Zang Yao does,

242
00:27:22,785 --> 00:27:24,705
and we don't share as many memories.

243
00:27:24,785 --> 00:27:27,265
Let me see the scar she mentioned.

244
00:27:27,345 --> 00:27:28,225
Shang Zhitao.

245
00:27:59,625 --> 00:28:00,705
Was Mount Tai fun?

246
00:28:04,105 --> 00:28:05,305
Yes.

247
00:28:06,385 --> 00:28:07,505
More fun than being with me?

248
00:28:22,305 --> 00:28:23,865
Do you hold a grudge over everything?

249
00:28:24,465 --> 00:28:25,745
I went with my roommates.

250
00:28:25,825 --> 00:28:27,945
We're very close,

251
00:28:28,025 --> 00:28:31,905
so we often do things together as a group.

252
00:28:35,585 --> 00:28:38,465
Are group outings more fun
than being with me?

253
00:28:39,065 --> 00:28:40,705
Are you fun?

254
00:28:41,825 --> 00:28:42,665
No.

255
00:28:43,345 --> 00:28:44,865
I'm not cheerful.

256
00:28:44,945 --> 00:28:48,825
I have no empathy and no soft side.

257
00:28:49,425 --> 00:28:51,385
At least you know yourself.

258
00:28:56,865 --> 00:28:57,865
You do have a soft side.

259
00:28:58,705 --> 00:29:00,185
You have friends,

260
00:29:00,785 --> 00:29:02,945
people you travel with,

261
00:29:03,025 --> 00:29:06,425
and even a childhood sweetheart.

262
00:29:06,505 --> 00:29:07,545
Isn't that right?

263
00:29:11,905 --> 00:29:12,745
Come.

264
00:29:21,425 --> 00:29:22,785
Zang Yao is a few years younger than me.

265
00:29:23,785 --> 00:29:25,185
She was sickly as a child,

266
00:29:25,265 --> 00:29:27,025
and my mom often
wrote prescriptions for her.

267
00:29:28,585 --> 00:29:29,905
Later, my parents went abroad.

268
00:29:31,065 --> 00:29:34,665
Her mom was a great cook,
so I often ate at their place.

269
00:29:36,425 --> 00:29:39,985
Your parents went abroad
without taking you?

270
00:29:41,625 --> 00:29:43,145
They went abroad for business.

271
00:29:43,745 --> 00:29:44,585
I didn't want to go.

272
00:29:44,665 --> 00:29:46,505
Are they back now?

273
00:29:48,265 --> 00:29:49,705
But we rarely get to see each other.

274
00:29:50,545 --> 00:29:51,745
Not even during Chinese New Year?

275
00:29:51,825 --> 00:29:53,705
It's almost here.

276
00:29:54,305 --> 00:29:56,585
Once the holiday starts,
I'm going back home.

277
00:29:59,145 --> 00:30:00,065
Shang Zhitao.

278
00:30:01,585 --> 00:30:03,065
When we see each other next year,

279
00:30:03,665 --> 00:30:05,785
I hope you'll call me something different.

280
00:30:08,345 --> 00:30:12,105
What do you want me to call you?

281
00:30:14,585 --> 00:30:15,945
Just call me Luan Nian.

282
00:30:20,945 --> 00:30:22,105
Luan…

283
00:30:24,265 --> 00:30:25,105
Luan Nian.

284
00:30:29,745 --> 00:30:30,665
Luan Nian.

285
00:30:33,865 --> 00:30:34,945
Don't tempt me.

286
00:30:36,625 --> 00:30:37,465
You're still sick.

287
00:30:50,905 --> 00:30:52,225
Actually,

288
00:30:53,345 --> 00:30:56,745
I think it's nice
just lying here like this,

289
00:30:58,865 --> 00:30:59,865
without doing anything.

290
00:31:04,665 --> 00:31:05,505
What's nice about it?

291
00:31:39,425 --> 00:31:40,385
TO-DO LIST
1. LEARN TO DRIVE 2. IMPROVE MY ENGLISH

292
00:31:40,465 --> 00:31:41,345
3. MAKE AT LEAST THREE FRIENDS
4. PASS PROBATION AND GET PROMOTED TO SAE

293
00:31:48,225 --> 00:31:50,945
5. CAREER GOAL: ACCOUNT MANAGER

294
00:31:52,985 --> 00:31:54,665
Did you get your year-end bonus?

295
00:31:55,745 --> 00:31:56,785
Check your email.

296
00:32:01,465 --> 00:32:02,705
That's so much money!

297
00:32:02,785 --> 00:32:04,585
The more, the better.

298
00:32:04,665 --> 00:32:05,705
Get a grip, silly.

299
00:32:06,545 --> 00:32:09,665
HR just announced
a company retreat in Phuket.

300
00:32:10,745 --> 00:32:12,265
Phuket?

301
00:32:15,585 --> 00:32:17,025
-Here.
-No, I can't.

302
00:32:17,105 --> 00:32:19,505
Just take it. Once your mentor,
always your mentor.

303
00:32:20,505 --> 00:32:21,345
Happy Chinese New Year.

304
00:32:33,105 --> 00:32:34,465
I'm grateful to Lime

305
00:32:36,665 --> 00:32:39,185
and to myself for working so hard.

306
00:32:39,265 --> 00:32:40,105
GOOD LUCK ALWAYS

307
00:32:40,185 --> 00:32:42,785
My job gave me the chance to work
at the forefront of the industry

308
00:32:43,385 --> 00:32:45,945
and see my efforts rewarded.

309
00:32:47,865 --> 00:32:48,745
I'm also grateful to Luan Nian.

310
00:32:50,225 --> 00:32:51,705
Thank you for your kindness,

311
00:32:52,345 --> 00:32:53,865
for always being strict,

312
00:32:53,945 --> 00:32:57,025
and for pushing me
to grow in my own way.

313
00:33:03,905 --> 00:33:06,625
JANUARY 2014, HARBIN

314
00:33:08,625 --> 00:33:10,225
I LOVE HARBIN

315
00:33:14,585 --> 00:33:15,625
CENTRAL AVENUE

316
00:33:15,705 --> 00:33:16,985
OLD COUPLE'S TAVERN

317
00:33:17,065 --> 00:33:19,265
Dad, I'll have a drink with you tonight.

318
00:33:20,025 --> 00:33:21,505
I'll join in too.

319
00:33:21,585 --> 00:33:22,825
You can barely hold your liquor.

320
00:33:22,905 --> 00:33:23,825
Just have a sip.

321
00:33:24,785 --> 00:33:25,905
-Cheers.
-Happy Chinese New Year!

322
00:33:25,985 --> 00:33:27,785
-Happy Chinese New Year!
-Happy Chinese New Year.

323
00:33:28,665 --> 00:33:30,185
Easy on the drinks.

324
00:33:30,265 --> 00:33:31,305
That's strong.

325
00:33:31,945 --> 00:33:35,305
Sweetheart, try the soup I made for you.

326
00:33:35,385 --> 00:33:36,585
It's been simmering all afternoon.

327
00:33:36,665 --> 00:33:38,305
It smells amazing.

328
00:33:38,825 --> 00:33:40,465
Here. Try it.

329
00:33:40,545 --> 00:33:42,025
All right.

330
00:33:42,105 --> 00:33:43,945
-You have some too.
-OK.

331
00:33:44,025 --> 00:33:45,865
Since when did you become
such a great cook?

332
00:33:45,945 --> 00:33:46,785
See?

333
00:33:46,865 --> 00:33:49,505
If Michelin knew,
they'd be giving you a star.

334
00:33:51,145 --> 00:33:55,465
Your auntie next door has a nephew
who's a programmer in Beijing.

335
00:33:55,545 --> 00:33:58,265
His hair is really thick.

336
00:33:58,345 --> 00:34:02,065
And his face is chiseled

337
00:34:02,145 --> 00:34:04,145
-like a European statue.
-Mom…

338
00:34:04,225 --> 00:34:05,105
Give it a rest.

339
00:34:05,185 --> 00:34:06,985
A European statue?

340
00:34:07,065 --> 00:34:09,705
Exactly. Besides, I want to focus on work.

341
00:34:09,784 --> 00:34:11,465
I'm not looking to date right now.

342
00:34:11,545 --> 00:34:13,625
-All right, let me name the dishes.
-Look at you…

343
00:34:13,705 --> 00:34:16,905
We've got Disanxian, sweet-and-sour pork,

344
00:34:16,985 --> 00:34:20,865
and your favorite, blood sausage!

345
00:34:20,945 --> 00:34:22,824
-Dig in.
-Eat.

346
00:34:27,105 --> 00:34:28,744
The Spring Festival
is always livelier at home.

347
00:34:28,824 --> 00:34:30,145
Everything feels so festive.

348
00:34:30,225 --> 00:34:32,065
-Stop watching and eat.
-Come on.

349
00:34:34,385 --> 00:34:35,425
Eat.

350
00:34:35,505 --> 00:34:36,705
LUAN NIAN, HAPPY CHINESE NEW YEAR
WISHING YOU ALL THE BEST THIS YEAR

351
00:34:36,784 --> 00:34:37,985
It smells amazing.

352
00:34:38,065 --> 00:34:39,225
Dig in, sweetheart.

353
00:34:39,304 --> 00:34:40,344
Have some blood sausage.

354
00:34:41,705 --> 00:34:43,185
Just looking at you makes me happy.

355
00:34:48,145 --> 00:34:49,505
Mom, this is so good.

356
00:34:49,585 --> 00:34:50,425
Try some.

357
00:34:56,465 --> 00:34:58,785
Luan Nian, Happy Chinese New Year.

358
00:34:59,465 --> 00:35:01,785
Wishing you all the best this year.

359
00:35:10,785 --> 00:35:13,305
Aren't you hot

360
00:35:13,385 --> 00:35:15,665
-wearing a turtleneck indoors?
-No.

361
00:35:16,585 --> 00:35:17,905
Here, have some fruit.

362
00:35:18,545 --> 00:35:19,385
Here.

363
00:35:23,185 --> 00:35:25,825
Are you hiding something from me?

364
00:35:26,465 --> 00:35:28,785
-Like what?
-Like what?

365
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:31,025
Don't walk away.

366
00:35:31,105 --> 00:35:32,505
I'm asking you.

367
00:35:32,585 --> 00:35:33,465
Go ahead.

368
00:35:34,305 --> 00:35:37,545
Are you seeing someone?

369
00:35:38,785 --> 00:35:40,425
Are you really that eager for me to date,

370
00:35:40,505 --> 00:35:42,705
get married, and give you a granddaughter?

371
00:35:43,385 --> 00:35:44,705
Why not a grandson?

372
00:35:46,025 --> 00:35:47,025
I prefer a girl.

373
00:35:47,105 --> 00:35:49,385
Of course, a granddaughter
would be better.

374
00:35:49,465 --> 00:35:50,385
I'd love that.

375
00:35:51,305 --> 00:35:53,385
Don't change the subject.
Are you seeing someone?

376
00:35:55,545 --> 00:35:56,785
I am.

377
00:35:57,385 --> 00:35:58,465
Really?

378
00:35:58,545 --> 00:36:00,905
What does she do?

379
00:36:00,985 --> 00:36:02,385
What's her personality like?

380
00:36:03,105 --> 00:36:04,065
What does she look like?

381
00:36:04,145 --> 00:36:07,065
She's easy on the eyes,
has a great personality,

382
00:36:07,145 --> 00:36:08,065
and works a regular office job.

383
00:36:08,665 --> 00:36:10,905
What kind of compliment
is "easy on the eyes"?

384
00:36:11,665 --> 00:36:14,105
It means she's pleasant to look at.

385
00:36:16,305 --> 00:36:18,385
Someone steady with a regular job is good.

386
00:36:19,145 --> 00:36:20,905
Don't date someone too domineering.

387
00:36:21,705 --> 00:36:22,785
We don't need that in this family.

388
00:36:24,505 --> 00:36:27,705
I'm choosing a girlfriend,
not a daughter-in-law for you.

389
00:36:28,305 --> 00:36:29,465
With your temper,

390
00:36:30,665 --> 00:36:31,625
you'll break up anyway.

391
00:36:32,705 --> 00:36:35,305
With your temper,
Mom still hasn't left you.

392
00:36:38,705 --> 00:36:40,145
All right, enough.

393
00:36:40,225 --> 00:36:41,425
This is good.

394
00:36:41,505 --> 00:36:44,345
I thought you'd be alone forever.

395
00:36:46,185 --> 00:36:48,385
A good personality matters.

396
00:36:49,025 --> 00:36:52,185
A girl may date you at first
because of your looks,

397
00:36:52,265 --> 00:36:56,425
but sooner or later,
she might not be able to stand you.

398
00:37:00,145 --> 00:37:03,225
By the way, Song Qiuhan's father told me

399
00:37:03,745 --> 00:37:06,065
your company was trying
to land Xingchi Auto as a client.

400
00:37:07,585 --> 00:37:08,665
We're working on it.

401
00:37:08,745 --> 00:37:10,185
How far along are you?

402
00:37:10,265 --> 00:37:14,145
In a deal of this size,
a proposal can only take you so far.

403
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:15,665
People are what make deals happen.

404
00:37:16,945 --> 00:37:18,505
I know how to manage client relationships.

405
00:37:18,585 --> 00:37:20,265
Don't trouble yourself with it, Mr. Luan.

406
00:37:23,105 --> 00:37:24,905
Don't let your talent make you arrogant.

407
00:37:25,585 --> 00:37:28,265
Creative ideas
aren't as valuable as you think.

408
00:37:28,345 --> 00:37:31,225
You need to spend more time
and put in more effort

409
00:37:31,305 --> 00:37:34,425
to understand what the client truly wants.

410
00:37:35,105 --> 00:37:35,985
Only then can you be sure of success.

411
00:37:36,065 --> 00:37:38,865
Why haven't you put this much effort
into Mom and me?

412
00:37:38,945 --> 00:37:40,785
Your own family
has never enjoyed that privilege.

413
00:37:41,385 --> 00:37:42,665
What nonsense are you talking about?

414
00:37:43,265 --> 00:37:44,825
I'm teaching you how to deal with people.

415
00:37:45,985 --> 00:37:48,505
If I hadn't been so strict
with you growing up

416
00:37:49,025 --> 00:37:50,225
and pushed you to become capable,

417
00:37:50,305 --> 00:37:51,905
would you be where you are today?

418
00:37:53,345 --> 00:37:55,025
Cacti can grow in the desert,

419
00:37:55,105 --> 00:37:57,905
but that doesn't mean
the desert is good for plants.

420
00:37:57,985 --> 00:37:59,905
-Hey you…
-All right, enough.

421
00:37:59,985 --> 00:38:00,825
Enough.

422
00:38:00,905 --> 00:38:03,025
It's Chinese New Year.
Why bring that up now?

423
00:38:03,105 --> 00:38:04,665
Our son is already doing very well.

424
00:38:04,745 --> 00:38:06,185
He doesn't need your guidance.

425
00:38:09,025 --> 00:38:10,065
Ignore him.

426
00:38:11,105 --> 00:38:12,665
Where are you going?

427
00:38:12,745 --> 00:38:14,785
Send me a photo of the girl.

428
00:38:14,865 --> 00:38:15,985
OK, I'll send you one.

429
00:38:16,065 --> 00:38:16,905
Hurry.

430
00:38:22,425 --> 00:38:23,425
Here it is.

431
00:38:26,945 --> 00:38:28,825
Look at what he sent me.

432
00:38:28,905 --> 00:38:30,345
Isn't that you?

433
00:38:30,425 --> 00:38:31,745
If he'd really wanted you to know,

434
00:38:32,425 --> 00:38:34,225
he would've sent you her photo long ago.

435
00:38:34,865 --> 00:38:37,105
You're always sticking
your nose into things.

436
00:38:37,185 --> 00:38:38,385
Can't I ask about my own son's

437
00:38:38,465 --> 00:38:39,905
-love life?
-What good does that do?

438
00:38:41,545 --> 00:38:43,385
He keeps brushing us off.

439
00:38:44,545 --> 00:38:47,705
You know perfectly well
he hates being interfered with

440
00:38:47,785 --> 00:38:49,865
and tied down, yet you still lecture him.

441
00:38:49,945 --> 00:38:51,905
Why can't I lecture him?

442
00:38:53,105 --> 00:38:56,345
He's been giving people
the silent treatment since childhood.

443
00:38:57,145 --> 00:38:58,185
What does he know about love?

444
00:38:58,265 --> 00:38:59,865
He knows nothing about it.

445
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:05,905
I've also heard
he can be arrogant with clients

446
00:39:05,985 --> 00:39:06,825
and incredibly difficult to deal with.

447
00:39:07,425 --> 00:39:08,585
Who would like someone like that?

448
00:39:09,185 --> 00:39:11,305
People don't like him,
and he doesn't like people.

449
00:39:11,385 --> 00:39:12,465
Isn't that just perfect?

450
00:39:12,545 --> 00:39:13,665
Perfect?

451
00:39:15,425 --> 00:39:16,265
You've spoiled him.

452
00:39:16,345 --> 00:39:18,185
Why are you so annoying?

453
00:39:18,265 --> 00:39:20,025
Our son is right.

454
00:39:20,105 --> 00:39:22,425
You should date someone
you enjoy looking at.

455
00:39:52,825 --> 00:39:54,585
Go easier on my neck next time.

456
00:39:58,225 --> 00:40:00,025
LUAN NIAN

457
00:40:07,305 --> 00:40:09,185
Why is it so quiet over there?

458
00:40:09,825 --> 00:40:12,345
The firecrackers have
already started here.

459
00:40:12,945 --> 00:40:14,425
My place is well soundproofed.

460
00:40:16,025 --> 00:40:17,225
What did you say?

461
00:40:17,945 --> 00:40:19,145
-Hello?
-Hello?

462
00:40:19,225 --> 00:40:21,545
-Sweetheart, come set off fireworks!
-Coming!

463
00:40:21,625 --> 00:40:24,425
I have to go. Bye.

464
00:40:34,545 --> 00:40:35,985
Happy Chinese New Year!

465
00:40:36,785 --> 00:40:39,265
Happy Chinese New Year!

466
00:40:39,345 --> 00:40:40,865
Happy Chinese New Year!

467
00:40:44,865 --> 00:40:46,305
They're beautiful.

468
00:40:48,305 --> 00:40:49,785
So beautiful!

469
00:40:52,185 --> 00:40:53,665
Happy Chinese New Year!

470
00:40:54,265 --> 00:40:55,105
Your red envelope.

471
00:40:57,225 --> 00:40:59,385
Come on. Family photo.

472
00:41:15,345 --> 00:41:16,545
Come back to Beijing soon.

473
00:41:58,545 --> 00:41:59,985
BOARDING GATES

474
00:42:04,265 --> 00:42:05,625
You've got to hand it to Luke.

475
00:42:05,705 --> 00:42:07,545
He picked Phuket for the company retreat.

476
00:42:07,625 --> 00:42:08,625
Yeah.

477
00:42:11,385 --> 00:42:12,345
Lumi.

478
00:42:13,705 --> 00:42:15,665
Why aren't you wearing
the dress I bought you?

479
00:42:15,745 --> 00:42:17,065
You're not wearing yours either.

480
00:42:17,145 --> 00:42:18,185
Mine's in my suitcase.

481
00:42:18,265 --> 00:42:19,145
So is mine.

482
00:42:19,225 --> 00:42:20,065
Alright.

483
00:42:20,145 --> 00:42:21,505
Then we'll change when we get there.

484
00:42:21,585 --> 00:42:22,425
Sit here.

485
00:42:23,145 --> 00:42:24,225
Where's your seat?

486
00:42:24,305 --> 00:42:25,505
-My seat…
-Look.

487
00:42:26,745 --> 00:42:27,785
Isn't that Luke?

488
00:42:29,465 --> 00:42:31,945
He's not joining us
on this southern tour, is he?

489
00:42:32,025 --> 00:42:34,185
Wouldn't that mean overtime in Phuket?

490
00:42:34,265 --> 00:42:35,425
No way.

491
00:42:35,505 --> 00:42:37,905
Why would he come on our company retreat?

492
00:42:37,985 --> 00:42:41,145
Probably because I'm the boss,
and I can go wherever I want.

493
00:42:44,545 --> 00:42:45,825
Where are you going?

494
00:42:47,025 --> 00:42:48,225
On the company retreat.

495
00:42:49,105 --> 00:42:50,185
You're coming with us?

496
00:42:50,265 --> 00:42:51,705
Is there a problem?

497
00:42:56,825 --> 00:42:57,865
Then…

498
00:42:58,425 --> 00:42:59,945
why aren't you in the first-class lounge?

499
00:43:00,025 --> 00:43:02,905
Since this is a company retreat,
there'll be no special treatment.

500
00:43:06,105 --> 00:43:06,945
Can I sit here?

501
00:43:08,265 --> 00:43:09,465
Let's move it.

502
00:43:10,785 --> 00:43:11,625
Go ahead.

503
00:43:18,345 --> 00:43:20,625
Could you be any more inconsiderate?

504
00:43:21,345 --> 00:43:23,585
How are we supposed
to have fun with you there?

505
00:43:24,865 --> 00:43:26,345
Then don't go.

506
00:43:38,065 --> 00:43:39,185
Why do you keep looking at me?

507
00:43:40,185 --> 00:43:42,145
It's not like I refused to get you
a business-class seat.

508
00:43:45,545 --> 00:43:47,265
I'll upgrade you now.

509
00:43:49,465 --> 00:43:51,665
Come on. Help me see
if we can upgrade his seat.

510
00:43:55,665 --> 00:43:58,065
Passengers traveling to Phuket,

511
00:43:58,145 --> 00:44:01,465
please gather your belongings
and prepare to board.

512
00:44:27,505 --> 00:44:28,345
You're awake?

513
00:44:30,785 --> 00:44:33,065
Here. Have some water.

514
00:44:49,465 --> 00:44:50,305
Your fever's gone down.

515
00:44:50,825 --> 00:44:52,785
If it comes back tomorrow,

516
00:44:53,305 --> 00:44:54,185
you'll still need a shot
to bring the fever down.

517
00:44:56,665 --> 00:44:58,345
Ask Alex for leave.

518
00:44:58,985 --> 00:45:00,345
Take five full days off.

519
00:45:02,665 --> 00:45:03,945
I don't need that many days.

520
00:45:06,665 --> 00:45:07,705
I still have work to do.

521
00:45:07,785 --> 00:45:10,705
Once the fever fries your brain,
you won't have to work at all.

522
00:45:14,665 --> 00:45:15,985
I'll rest at home.

523
00:45:32,145 --> 00:45:33,545
I know you have something to say.

524
00:45:34,745 --> 00:45:35,585
I'm going out for a while.

525
00:45:35,665 --> 00:45:38,665
Think about how you want to say it
before I get back.
